; The entry calls function 1 on four valid elements, then calls it again
; with a failure on the fourth. The test varies the final layout in block 7
; to reach the reference check, class cast, or three-way selector.
; Layouts 0, 1, and 2 form a class hierarchy. Function 1 reads the least
; specific type, checks layout 1 through an assignment from lanes, then
; casts to layout 2. Its scalar slot 8 receives the previous index. After
; each failing check, that slot is overwritten before a read or discarded
; on exit. Output lane values and exit selectors are checked at runtime.
